All findings confirmed. Here is the report.

## Summary

The PTY subsystem lives in `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts` (dedicated PTY manager/service module — no class, but a module-level singleton with a private `Map`), wired to IPC via `src/main/ipc/ptyIpc.ts`. It uses `node-pty` (lazy-loaded).

### 1. Live PTY session tracking

`/home/namastex/prod/genie-desktop/src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:38`

```ts
const ptys = new Map<string, PtyRecord>();
```

Backing record type, `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:21-36`:

```ts
interface PtyRecord {
  proc: any; // IPty from node-pty
  cwd: string;
  isDirectSpawn: boolean;
  owner: WebContents | null;
  kind: PtyKind;          // 'agent' | 'shell' | 'tui' | 'service'
  taskId: string | null;
  featureId: string | null;
  mirror: TerminalMirror | null;
}
```

The map is keyed by session/pty id (e.g. bare task id for agent PTYs, `shell:<taskId>[:N]` for shell PTYs). Entries are inserted at spawn time (`ptys.set(...)` at lines 522, 645, 906) and removed on exit/kill (`ptys.delete(...)` at lines 437, 551, 665, 768/780, 814, 925). Lookup helpers: `hasPty` (line 182-184) and `listForTask` (lines 840-852, filters by `taskId`/`kind`/`featureId`).

### 2. Terminal resize → `pty.resize()`

Renderer → preload → IPC → manager → `node-pty`:

- Renderer call sites (`src/renderer/terminal/TerminalSessionManager.ts:940-942, 1002`):
```ts
window.electronAPI.ptyResize({ id: this.id, cols, rows: dims.rows });
```
- Preload bridge, `src/main/preload.ts:72-73`:
```ts
ptyResize: (args: { id: string; cols: number; rows: number }) =>
  ipcRenderer.send('pty:resize', args),
```
- IPC handler, `src/main/ipc/ptyIpc.ts:103-111`:
```ts
ipcMain.on('pty:resize', (_event, args: { id: string; cols: number; rows: number }) => {
  const v = parseArgsSafe(
    'pty:resize',
    z.looseObject({ id: z.string(), cols: z.number(), rows: z.number() }),
    args,
  );
  if (v === undefined) return;
  resizePty(args.id, args.cols, args.rows);
});
```
- Manager function that actually calls `proc.resize`, `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:692-705`:
```ts
export function resizePty(id: string, cols: number, rows: number): void {
  const record = ptys.get(id);
  if (record) {
    record.mirror?.resize(cols, rows);
    try {
      record.proc.resize(cols, rows);
    } catch {
      // EBADF can happen during transitions
    }
  }
}
```

### 3. PTY shutdown/kill — graceful SIGTERM then SIGKILL after a timeout

Timeout constant, `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:707-708`:

```ts
// Grace window for a SIGTERM'd child to flush and exit before we force SIGKILL.
const GRACEFUL_KILL_TIMEOUT_MS = 3000;
```

Core kill function, `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:727-763`:

```ts
function gracefulKillProc(proc: KillableProc, timeoutMs = GRACEFUL_KILL_TIMEOUT_MS): Promise<void> {
  return new Promise<void>((resolve) => {
    let settled = false;
    let timer: ReturnType<typeof setTimeout> | null = null;
    let disposable: { dispose: () => void } | null = null;
    const finish = () => { ... };
    try {
      disposable = proc.onExit(() => finish());
    } catch { /* proc doesn't expose onExit */ }
    timer = setTimeout(() => {
      try {
        proc.kill('SIGKILL');
      } catch { /* already dead */ }
      finish();
    }, timeoutMs);
    try {
      proc.kill('SIGTERM');
    } catch {
      finish();
    }
  });
}
```

So: `SIGTERM` is sent immediately; if the process hasn't emitted `onExit` within 3000ms (`GRACEFUL_KILL_TIMEOUT_MS`, `ptyManager.ts:708`), `SIGKILL` is sent. The comment above it (`ptyManager.ts:710-719`) explains *why*: node-pty's bare `.kill()` sends `SIGHUP` which Claude Code doesn't trap, losing the in-memory session tail — SIGTERM+wait lets it persist first.

Call sites/wrappers around it:
- `killPtyInternal` (single PTY teardown + kill), `ptyManager.ts:777-782`
- `killPty` (fire-and-forget), `ptyManager.ts:789-791`
- `killPtyAwait` (awaits actual exit — used before respawn to avoid a two-writer race on the session jsonl), `ptyManager.ts:799-801`
- `killAll` (app quit — kills every tracked PTY in parallel), `ptyManager.ts:808-818`
- `killByOwner` (window-close cleanup for one `WebContents`), `ptyManager.ts:825-832`

IPC exposure: `pty:kill` (fire-and-forget, `src/main/ipc/ptyIpc.ts:113-117`) and `pty:kill-await` (awaited, `ptyIpc.ts:122-130`).

Tests exercising this: `src/main/services/__tests__/ptyManager.gracefulKill.test.ts`, `src/main/services/__tests__/ptyManager.exit.test.ts`.

### 4. Spawn environment / cwd / shell selection

Three separate spawn call sites, all lazy-loading `node-pty` via `getPty()` (`ptyManager.ts:201-216`, `require('node-pty')` at line 207):

**a) Agent (Claude) PTY** — `startDirectPty`, spawn call at `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:503-509`:
```ts
const pty = getPty();
const proc = pty.spawn(spawnPlan.command, spawnPlan.args, {
  name: 'xterm-256color',
  cols: options.cols,
  rows: options.rows,
  cwd: spawnPlan.cwd,
  env: spawnPlan.env,
});
```
`spawnPlan` (command/args/cwd/env) is built by an **agent adapter** (`adapter.buildSpawn(...)`, called at `ptyManager.ts:484-496`), which in turn calls `buildDirectEnv` (see below). Binary resolution is adapter-driven (`adapter.resolveBinary()`, line 458).

**b) Interactive shell PTY** — `startPty`, spawn call at `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:582-623`:
```ts
const isWin = process.platform === 'win32';
const shell = isWin ? 'powershell.exe' : process.env.SHELL || '/bin/bash';
const args = isWin ? ['-NoLogo'] : ['-i'];   // interactive, NOT login (perf: skips ~0.5s of .zprofile/.zlogin)

const env = { ...process.env };
delete env.ELECTRON_RUN_AS_NODE;
delete env.ELECTRON_NO_ATTACH_CONSOLE;

if (!isWin) {
  if (process.platform === 'darwin') env.TERM_PROGRAM = 'Apple_Terminal'; // OSC7 cwd reporting
  if (shell.endsWith('/zsh') || shell === 'zsh') env.ZDOTDIR = ensureShellConfig(); // custom prompt injection
}

for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(WorkspacePortsRuntime.getEnvForWorktree(options.cwd))) {
  env[key] = value;   // per-task port env (FRONTEND_PORT etc.)
}

const proc = pty.spawn(shell, args, {
  name: 'xterm-256color',
  cols: options.cols,
  rows: options.rows,
  cwd: options.cwd,
  env: env as Record<string, string>,
});
```

**c) Arbitrary side-car command PTY** (e.g. ports-onboarding TUI) — `startCommandPty`, spawn call at `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:886-893`:
```ts
const proc = pty.spawn(options.command, options.args, {
  name: 'xterm-256color',
  cols: options.cols,
  rows: options.rows,
  cwd: options.cwd,
  env: { ...process.env, ...(options.env ?? {}) } as Record<string, string>,
});
```

**Shared env builder** for direct/agent spawns — `buildDirectEnv(isDark, cwd)`, `src/main/services/ptyManager.ts:231-340`. Notable behaviors:
- `syncShellEnv` flag (line 119, setter `setSyncShellEnv` line 190-192) toggles between a minimal base env (default) and full `process.env` inheritance (line 233-235).
- PATH is merged with an rtk-managed bin dir if present, via `RtkService.getManagedBinDirForPath()` and `prependUnique()` (lines 239-242, 348-353).
- Always sets `TERM_PROGRAM='dash'`, `HOME`, `PATH`, `COLORFGBG` (dark/light aware) — lines 244-252.
- Windows branch (lines 254-277) forwards `APPDATA`, `LOCALAPPDATA`, `USERPROFILE`, `TEMP`, `TMP`, `SystemRoot`/`SYSTEMROOT`, `SystemDrive`, `WINDIR`, `COMSPEC`, `PATHEXT`, `COMPUTERNAME`, `USERDOMAIN`, `ProgramFiles`.
- Unix branch (lines 278-282) sets `TERM='xterm-256color'`, `COLORTERM='truecolor'`, `USER`.
- When `syncShellEnv` is off, auth passthrough of `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `GH_TOKEN`, `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `HTTP(S)_PROXY`/`NO_PROXY` (both cases) — lines 284-303.
- User-configured env vars (`claudeEnvVars`, settable via `setClaudeEnvVars`, line 186-188) are merged in, guarded by a reserved-key blocklist:
```ts
const RESERVED_ENV_KEYS = new Set([
  'PATH', 'HOME', 'USER', 'TERM', 'COLORTERM', 'TERM_PROGRAM', 'COLORFGBG',
  'DASH_HOOK_PORT',
]);  // ptyManager.ts:127-138
```
- Per-task port env vars merged from `WorkspacePortsRuntime.getEnvForWorktree(cwd)` (lines 320-324).
- `CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=1` always set to disable Claude Code's own viewport scrolling (line 327) — Dash manages the terminal viewport itself.
- `DASH_HOOK_PORT` set last (wins over inherited value) when `hookServer.port !== 0`, so hook curl commands in `settings.local.json` (written by `writeHookSettings`, from `./ptyHookSettings`) route back to the app's local HookServer (lines 329-337).

Related file for shell prompt customization referenced above: `/home/namastex/prod/genie-desktop/src/main/services/ptyShellConfig.ts` (`ensureShellConfig()` — sets up `ZDOTDIR` for the injected zsh prompt).

